# Backgrounds
@scenario tutorial_lesson_04
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@background alternate assets/tutorial/white.png
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code normal]
[set tutorial_source scripts/definitions/characters.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt background]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: The white background is a project asset. This lesson refers to it by the ID {b}room{/b}.
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/04_images_and_backgrounds.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt select_backdrop]
ginger: The shared definitions pair room with the white PNG. This lesson declares its own ID, alternate. Advance to select it with the bg command.
# region select_backdrop
[bg alternate]
ginger: Both IDs point to the same PNG, so the screen looks the same. Change alternate's path to another image and replay to see the switch.
# endregion
[bg room]
ginger: Follow room through the two files. The declaration supplies a path. The background command supplies the ID. A file rename affects the path even if every command still uses the same ID.
ginger: Two IDs can point to one PNG. That gives you a way to test a second reference before adding any new artwork to the project.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Trace a background reference -> practice
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: What goes after bg?
> The name of the current speaker. -> retry
> The ID declared for the backdrop. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: The speaker ID is used on dialogue lines. Look up the ID on the background declaration.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Use the declared background ID. Editing its asset path updates every place that selects that ID.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_04]
[flag tutorial_done_04]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_2]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/definitions/characters.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt background]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Find room in the shared definitions. Leave its path alone so the other lessons keep their white backdrop.
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/04_images_and_backgrounds.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt select_backdrop]
ginger: Point the alternate declaration in this lesson at a visibly different project image. Start from the beginning and advance to the highlighted bg command.
ginger: Change [bg alternate] to [bg room] and run it again. Both cues should now select the shared white backdrop.
ginger: For a packaged project, check the path from the asset root and the filename's case. An absolute path to an image on your own desktop cannot travel with the project.
@label practice_question
ginger: Two lessons use room. Only this one should get the alternate backdrop. Which edit has the right scope?
> Replace the file mapped to room. -> practice_hint
> Add a second ID and use it in this lesson. -> practice_result
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: Both lessons resolve room through the same declaration. Replacing its image changes the result for both callers.
[jump practice_question]
@label practice_result
ginger: The new ID makes the choice local to the lesson. Run the other lesson as a control and check that room still resolves to the white PNG.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the exercise again -> practice
> Back to topics -> return_hub
